{{also|kamel}}
==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|de|Kameel||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{inh+|de|gmh|kemel}}, {{m|gmh|kemmel}}, {{m|gmh|kembel}}, borrowed during the Crusades from {{der|de|gkm|κάμηλος}}, probably in part also from {{der|de|ar|جَمَل}}, which best explains the ''e''-vocalism (as Arabic ''a'' is {{IPAchar|[æ]}} or even {{IPAchar|[ɛ]}} in this word). The modern form with final stress is a 16th-century learned alteration after {{der|de|la|camēlus}}, itself from {{der|de|grc|-}}, from a {{der|de|sem|-}} language. It was accordingly mostly spelt {{m|de||Kameel}} until the early 20th century (a spelling then abolished after words like {{m|de|Klientel}}, {{m|de|parallel}}). An older term for the animal was {{noncog|goh|olbenta}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/kaˈmeːl/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Kamel.ogg}}
* {{rhymes|de|eːl}}

